{"name":"Early Cyber","title":"Early Cyber","revision":234453,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Early_Cyber","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Early Cyber was an aesthetic movement that was most predominant from the mid-1980s to mid-1990s, with early examples present as early as the 1970s. This aesthetic consisted of harsh pixelated thermographic imagery with warped fonts made newly possible through the proliferation of the first wave of desktop publishing and image manipulation software, often with Cyberpunk themes. This aesthetic also featured early usage of CGI. It had overlap with the 90s Cool, Cyberdelia, Silicon Dreams, Factory Pomo, and Corporate Gen-X Cyber aesthetics."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"By the late 1990s, this aesthetic had evolved into more polished/conventional aesthetics such as Y2K Futurism and Metalheart."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Various sorts of early computer graphics and techniques that were becoming more broadly available."},{"kind":"list","text":"Dot matrix patterns"},{"kind":"list","text":"Thermographic or artificial/altered color imagery"},{"kind":"list","text":"Posterization and solarization effects"},{"kind":"list","text":"Heavy pixelation effects"},{"kind":"list","text":"Early greenscreen"},{"kind":"list","text":"Kaleidoscope effects"},{"kind":"list","text":"Head-up displays"},{"kind":"list","text":"Squash, stretch and other warping effects (e.g. fisheye)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Fractals"},{"kind":"list","text":"Water-drop tools"},{"kind":"list","text":"Glow effects"},{"kind":"list","text":"Some amounts of CGI imagery, though unlike Silicon Dreams', Early Cyber's use of 3D graphics is usually more abstract"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Television"},{"kind":"list","text":"Doctor Who (Peter Davison and Colin Baker eras 1982-1986)"},{"kind":"list","text":"ITV's The Chart Show sponsored by Twix (1986-1998)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Red Dwarf (1988-1999)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Boy from Andromeda (1991)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Finders Keepers/The Finder (1991-1992)"},{"kind":"list","text":"GamesMaster intro (1992-1998)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Scavengers game show (1994-1995)"},{"kind":"list","text":"ReBoot (1994)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Beast Wars: Transformers (1996)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Music"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Don't Stop 'til You Get Enough\" by Michael Jackson (1979)"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"I Want Candy\" by Bow Wow (1982)"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Time Stand Still\" by Rush (1987)"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Pump Up the Jam\" by Technotronic (1989)"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"In Yer Face\" by 808 State (1991)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Don't You Want Me by Felix (1992)"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Rhythm Is a Dancer\" by Snap (1992)"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Tribal Dance\" by 2 Unlimited (1993)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Film"},{"kind":"list","text":"Aliens (1986) - Possibly Proto-Early Cyber"},{"kind":"list","text":"Max Headroom: 20 Minutes into the Future (1985)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Circuitry Man (1990)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hardware (1990)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Lawnmower Man (1992)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cyborg Cop (1993)"},{"kind":"list","text":"TekWar (1993-1995)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cyber Tracker (1994)"},{"kind":"list","text":"T-Force (1994)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hackers (1995)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Net (1995)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hologram Man (1995)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Technofear/Shadow Warriors (1995)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Johnny Mnemonic (1995)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Batman Forever (1995)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Batman & Robin (1997)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Vendors"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"TBD"}],"contentStatus":"full-source","images":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/7/78/R-1078773-1288700427.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20241118024752","caption":"R-1078773-1288700427","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:R-1078773-1288700427.jpg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0331-1.webp","localAvailable":true},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/0/08/Original_0678ea8578a59aa69a2067117915f89b.png/revision/latest?cb=20241118223335","caption":"John Devereaux – Wired (1988)","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:Original_0678ea8578a59aa69a2067117915f89b.png","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0331-2.webp","localAvailable":true}]}